WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.170
My cousin bought a cheap camera

2
00:00:02.170 --> 00:00:03.810
to watch her shop at night.

3
00:00:04.490 --> 00:00:07.270
A week later, a friend sent her a link.

4
00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.960
It was her shop, live, on a

5
00:00:10.960 --> 00:00:12.760
website anyone could open.

6
00:00:13.380 --> 00:00:15.960
She'd never changed the camera's password.

7
00:00:17.460 --> 00:00:20.160
Today: the Internet of Things, and

8
00:00:20.160 --> 00:00:21.380
how to stay safe with it.

9
00:00:22.580 --> 00:00:25.280
The Internet of Things means everyday

10
00:00:25.280 --> 00:00:27.220
things connected to a network.

11
00:00:27.970 --> 00:00:31.170
Each one has three parts: a sensor to

12
00:00:31.170 --> 00:00:35.050
notice, a small computer to decide, and a

13
00:00:35.050 --> 00:00:36.670
connection to send and receive.

14
00:00:37.980 --> 00:00:40.980
At home: a smart TV, a gate camera,

15
00:00:41.460 --> 00:00:42.780
a watch that counts steps.

16
00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:45.260
At school: a weather station

17
00:00:45.260 --> 00:00:46.180
that sends readings.

18
00:00:47.010 --> 00:00:49.950
In town: buses you can follow on a map.

19
00:00:50.620 --> 00:00:52.560
On farms: soil sensors

20
00:00:52.560 --> 00:00:53.940
that text the farmer.

21
00:00:55.230 --> 00:00:55.810
Quick check!

22
00:00:56.600 --> 00:00:59.880
Our school's weather station has sensors

23
00:00:59.880 --> 00:01:04.080
for rain and heat, and a small computer.

24
00:01:04.760 --> 00:01:06.440
What would make it part of

25
00:01:06.440 --> 00:01:08.100
the Internet of Things?

26
00:01:09.540 --> 00:01:11.460
A connection that sends its readings.

27
00:01:12.300 --> 00:01:14.220
Sensors and a small computer

28
00:01:14.220 --> 00:01:15.500
make a clever gadget.

29
00:01:16.210 --> 00:01:18.870
Add Wi-Fi, a mobile network or a

30
00:01:18.870 --> 00:01:20.530
radio link, and the readings

31
00:01:20.530 --> 00:01:22.070
reach a phone far away.

32
00:01:23.270 --> 00:01:24.830
Remember that shop camera?

33
00:01:25.490 --> 00:01:27.450
Many devices leave the factory with

34
00:01:27.450 --> 00:01:29.990
an easy password, like admin.

35
00:01:30.710 --> 00:01:32.590
Attackers keep lists of them.

36
00:01:33.180 --> 00:01:36.020
In twenty sixteen, a program called Mirai

37
00:01:36.020 --> 00:01:38.500
used about sixty of them to take over

38
00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:40.840
hundreds of thousands of cameras and

39
00:01:40.840 --> 00:01:41.340
routers.

40
00:01:42.570 --> 00:01:44.450
So, with an adult, make

41
00:01:44.450 --> 00:01:46.250
every new device safe.

42
00:01:46.960 --> 00:01:48.360
Change the factory password

43
00:01:48.360 --> 00:01:50.260
to a long new one.

44
00:01:50.870 --> 00:01:53.490
Turn on updates, which fix weak spots.

45
00:01:54.250 --> 00:01:56.510
And switch off features you don't use.

46
00:01:57.830 --> 00:02:00.650
Apps ask for permissions: your camera,

47
00:02:01.090 --> 00:02:03.650
microphone, location or contacts.

48
00:02:04.450 --> 00:02:07.430
Before you tap Allow, ask: does

49
00:02:07.430 --> 00:02:08.770
it need this for its job?

50
00:02:09.400 --> 00:02:10.700
A torch app needs the

51
00:02:10.700 --> 00:02:12.200
flash, not your contacts.

52
00:02:13.070 --> 00:02:15.030
You can change permissions any time.

53
00:02:16.230 --> 00:02:17.890
Connected things share, too.

54
00:02:18.550 --> 00:02:21.170
A photo can carry the place it was taken.

55
00:02:21.810 --> 00:02:23.230
A fitness watch can map

56
00:02:23.230 --> 00:02:23.970
your walk to school.

57
00:02:24.680 --> 00:02:27.660
So share less, and keep accounts private.

58
00:02:29.000 --> 00:02:29.760
Your turn.

59
00:02:30.380 --> 00:02:32.760
A free puzzle game asks for your

60
00:02:32.760 --> 00:02:35.340
microphone, your contacts and your

61
00:02:35.340 --> 00:02:35.700
location.

62
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:37.480
What do you allow?

63
00:02:38.820 --> 00:02:41.000
None of them: a puzzle needs no

64
00:02:41.000 --> 00:02:43.400
microphone, contacts or location.

65
00:02:44.170 --> 00:02:46.750
Remember: the Internet of Things is

66
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:49.830
things that sense, decide and connect.

67
00:02:50.520 --> 00:02:52.700
Change factory passwords and

68
00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.040
keep devices updated.

69
00:02:54.730 --> 00:02:56.490
Allow only what an app

70
00:02:56.490 --> 00:02:58.350
needs, and share less.

71
00:02:59.700 --> 00:03:01.740
Try it tomorrow: with an adult,

72
00:03:02.120 --> 00:03:04.320
list the connected things at home,

73
00:03:04.580 --> 00:03:06.400
from the router to the TV.

74
00:03:07.080 --> 00:03:08.860
Was each one's factory

75
00:03:08.860 --> 00:03:10.400
password ever changed?

76
00:03:11.180 --> 00:03:14.320
Then open one app's permissions, and

77
00:03:14.320 --> 00:03:15.880
switch off one it doesn't need.
